say where the resources directory resolved to

The url this returns is RELATIVE to the bundle by construction, so what a caller gets depends
entirely on whether it resolves against the base. -[NSBundle resourcePath] is [[self resourceURL]
path], and for wxWidgets that one string is the WHOLE translation search path: wxStandardPaths
GetResourcesDir is [[NSBundle mainBundle] resourcePath], read out of the shipping binary.

Bounded to twenty lines and on the existing CIDER_TRACE_MAINBUNDLE gate, next to the line that
already says what the main bundle was derived from.

MEASURED for Money Manager EX, and it was RIGHT, which is what let the search move on to the table
that was drawing the answer three pixels wide (#213):

  mainbundle: processPath=/Applications/mmex.app/Contents/MacOS/mmex bundleURL=/Applications/mmex.app
  mainbundle: resources version=2 path=/Applications/mmex.app/Contents/Resources
--- a/CFBundle.c
+++ b/CFBundle.c
@@ -1522,7 +1522,28 @@
 }
 
 CF_EXPORT CFURLRef CFBundleCopyResourcesDirectoryURL(CFBundleRef bundle) {
-    return _CFBundleCopyResourcesDirectoryURLInDirectory(bundle->_url, bundle->_version);
+    CFURLRef result = _CFBundleCopyResourcesDirectoryURLInDirectory(bundle->_url, bundle->_version);
+
+    /* The url is RELATIVE to the bundle by construction, so what a caller gets depends entirely on
+     * whether it resolves against the base. Print the resolved path, which is what -[NSBundle
+     * resourcePath] answers and what wxWidgets uses as its whole translation search path (#213). */
+    if (getenv("CIDER_TRACE_MAINBUNDLE")) {
+        static int printed;
+
+        if (printed < 20) {
+            CFURLRef absolute = result ? CFURLCopyAbsoluteURL(result) : NULL;
+            CFStringRef path = absolute ? CFURLCopyFileSystemPath(absolute, PLATFORM_PATH_STYLE) : NULL;
+            char buf[1024] = "(none)";
+
+            printed++;
+            if (path) CFStringGetCString(path, buf, sizeof(buf), kCFStringEncodingUTF8);
+            fprintf(stderr, "mainbundle: resources version=%d path=%s\n", (int) bundle->_version, buf);
+            fflush(stderr);
+            if (path) CFRelease(path);
+            if (absolute) CFRelease(absolute);
+        }
+    }
+    return result;
 }
 
